Falsifies `generational_table::verification::contains_key_and_get_agree_on_any_name`.

The defect: `contains_key` asks whether the name's slot is occupied and never compares the
generation. For every name the table holds it answers correctly, so a test that only asks about
live names and garbage slots passes.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(t.contains_key(probe), t.get(probe).is_some())`, on
any word whose slot is occupied and whose generation is not that slot's: a removed name whose
slot took a new entry is reported as a key.
diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
index 2214a94..3316e92 100644
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -302,7 +302,9 @@ impl<T, const N: usize> Table<T, N> {
     /// Whether `name` resolves to a live entry: [`get`](Self::get) without the reference. `false`
     /// for a removed name, a name from a previous occupant of the slot, or garbage.
     pub fn contains_key(&self, name: EntryName<T>) -> bool {
-        self.slot_of(name).is_some()
+        self.slots
+            .get(Self::unpack(name).0 as usize)
+            .is_some_and(Option::is_some)
     }
 
     /// [`get`](Self::get), mutably.
